{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You shall not show partiality in judgment.</b> This refers to the one appointed to seat judges — that he not say, 'So-and-so is handsome or a warrior, I shall seat him as judge'; 'So-and-so is my relative, I shall seat him as judge in the city' — and he is not versed in laws, with the result that he obligates the innocent and acquits the guilty. I hold it against the one who appointed him as though he himself showed partiality in judgment." "<b>As the small so the great you shall hear.</b> A case involving a perutah should be as dear to you as a case involving a hundred maneh — for if it came before you first, you must not send it away to a later slot. Another interpretation — <b>as the small so the great you shall hear</b> — as the Targum renders: that you not say, 'This one is poor and the other is rich, and I am commanded to sustain him — I will acquit the poor man, and so he will be sustained lawfully.' Another interpretation — that you not say, 'How can I impair the honor of this rich man over a dinar? I will acquit him now, and when he goes outside I will say to him: Give it to him, for you owe him' (there)." "<b>You shall not be afraid before any man.</b> You shall not fear. Another interpretation — <b>you shall not be afraid</b> — you shall not hold back your words because of any man — the sense of ״אֹגֵר בַּקַּיִץ״ (Proverbs 10)." "<b>For the judgment is Elohim's.</b> What you take from this one unlawfully — you compel Me to restore it to him; the result is that you have bent the judgment against Me (Sanhedrin 8)." "<b>You shall bring near to me.</b> Because of this matter the judgment of the daughters of Tzelofchad was hidden from him (there). And similarly Samuel said to Saul (I Samuel 9) ״אָנֹכִי הָרֹאֶה״ — the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: By your life, I will inform you that you do not see. And when did He inform him? When he came to anoint David (I Samuel 16): ״וַיַּרְא אֶת אֱלִיאָב וַיֹּאמֶר אַךְ נֶגֶד ה׳ מְשִׁיחוֹ״ — the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: And did you not say ״אָנֹכִי הָרֹאֶה״? ״אַל תַּבֵּט אֶל מַרְאֵהוּ״ (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:33.440558350Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}